<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dresden Frauenkirche</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1726–1743</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Frauenkirche in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a> is a Lutheran church built between 1726 and 1743 to designs by George Bähr and crowned by a great stone dome, a landmark of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> Dresden. Destroyed in the Allied bombing of February 1945, it remained a ruin and war memorial throughout the East German period and was rebuilt from 1994 to 2005, using original stones where possible.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dresden-frauenkirche.jpg" alt="Dresden Frauenkirche" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Netopyr · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:100130_150006_Dresden_Frauenkirche_winter_blue_sky-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
